"Where is AI?"


Students identify AI systems they interact with every day and classify:
What the AI does
What data it uses
What business problem it solves
Who benefits
What could go wrong

ChatGPT:
1. It's a generative AI, where you can generate anything, and it can answer any question you have.
2. It uses trillions of data from the internet, and it collects and trains from any and all data from publicly accessible things, and when you type out a question it queries, through the world wide web and it produces you the answer to that question.
3. It allows any one and any business to get answers quickly, rather than waiting hours or days for someone who specializes into that type of problem to actually respond.
4. Generally anyone can benefit from using this, like students, business owners, and everyday users.
5. It can hallucinate which can provide you the wrong information and mostly likely give you the wrong answer to something. People can also jailbreak it to allow them to send prompts which are not good and can cause harm.

TikTok:
1. TikTok I believe has built-in algorithms that look at each user, and recommend the user those videos that they're interested in.
2. I believe it uses comments, likes, shares, bookmarks, watch time, and followed accounts, and it feeds that to the person who is using their app.
3. It solves the idea of being bored, and also helps businesses push their stuff out in advertisements that are ran by themselves and creators on the platform.
4. Many people benefit from this, like business owners, creators, and normal users who use TikTok.
5. Many things can go wrong, like it can be very addiciting where people scroll on TikTok for hours upon hours reducing their attention span, it can collect more personal information than the user agreed upon, and it could possibly show harmful and weird videos to young audiences.
